WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.735
Guide seven: Shorts.

2
00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.666
Every video can give you up to five

3
00:00:03.666 --> 00:00:06.354
vertical clips, and you tick which ones.

4
00:00:06.954 --> 00:00:08.701
First, once per channel, you pick

5
00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.249
how long your Shorts can be:

6
00:00:10.249 --> 00:00:11.997
up to sixty seconds, ninety seconds

7
00:00:11.997 --> 00:00:13.145
or three minutes.

8
00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:14.593
A Short that's too long for a

9
00:00:14.593 --> 00:00:16.791
platform skips it, and you're told.

10
00:00:17.391 --> 00:00:19.388
Every finished video can feed one to

11
00:00:19.388 --> 00:00:20.812
five vertical Shorts.

12
00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:22.340
Say: make EP1's Shorts.

13
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.027
Your assistant proposes the best

14
00:00:24.027 --> 00:00:26.444
moments, each with a one-line reason.

15
00:00:27.044 --> 00:00:29.255
Tick the ones you want, up to five.

16
00:00:29.255 --> 00:00:31.058
Each one starts and ends on a whole

17
00:00:31.058 --> 00:00:32.448
sentence, and it says which

18
00:00:32.448 --> 00:00:34.504
platforms its length can go to.

19
00:00:35.104 --> 00:00:36.750
The Shorts then show up in your

20
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.196
Studio. Open the video, click

21
00:00:38.196 --> 00:00:39.742
Shorts, and play them.

22
00:00:40.342 --> 00:00:41.554
Don't like one?

23
00:00:41.554 --> 00:00:43.249
Click Change the Shorts, and say

24
00:00:43.249 --> 00:00:44.511
what to change.

25
00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.176
You choose where Shorts go, once, in

26
00:00:47.176 --> 00:00:49.031
Set up: YouTube Shorts, and if you

27
00:00:49.031 --> 00:00:50.942
like TikTok, Instagram, X, Facebook

28
00:00:50.942 --> 00:00:52.074
and Threads.

29
00:00:52.674 --> 00:00:54.763
Posting happens in your own browser

30
00:00:54.763 --> 00:00:57.130
and each post waits for your yes.

31
00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.955
Next: saying yes to publish, and

32
00:00:59.955 --> 00:01:01.167
autopilot.
